                <pb facs="0451" n="381" sameAs="frus:frus1934v04/pg381"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/2199: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dearing</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-04-12T15:00:00-05:00">April 12, 1934—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>48. Department’s telegram 31, April 11, 3 p.m. Leticia—American aviators.
                    Minister of Foreign Affairs takes Department’s message as a completely friendly
                    expression, saying our Government’s attitude gives the greatest satisfaction and
                    that he is reporting it to President, Cabinet, and consultative board. He also
                    has report from Freyre.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dearing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
